@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Customer Contact Role API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality in relation to Customer Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Customer Role  |
	| Optional Account Customer Role |

Scenario: Assign account customer contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to account customer contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles
	| Default Account Customer Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign non existent account customer contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to non existent account customer contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a nested field for the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         | |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region               | United States                        | |
	| Status               | Active                               | |
	| Tier                 | T4                                   | |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign non existent account customer contact role and account customer contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to existent and non existent account customer contact roles on accounts.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I rename the first contact role nested field variable
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	And I create a nested field for the contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And I rename the second contact role nested field variable
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a nested field for the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField1},${staticContactRolesNestedField2}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         | |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region               | United States                        | |
	| Status               | Active                               | |
	| Tier                 | T4                                   | |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"

