Scenario: View account modified date value after contact updates
	Koroneiki account modified date value should update after a contact change

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I obtain the date modified value for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I rename the first account date modified value
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Customer Role |
	And I obtain the date modified value for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I rename the second account date modified value
	Then the account date modified value "${staticAccountDateModified1Value1}" should be different from the "${staticAccountDateModified1Value2}"
	When I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role"
	When I obtain the date modified value for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I rename the third account date modified value
	Then the account date modified value "${staticAccountDateModifiedValue2}" should be different from the "${accountDateModifiedValue3}"
	When I remove the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" from the following roles	
	| Optional Account Customer Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role"
	When I obtain the date modified value for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I rename the fourth account date modified value
	And the account date modified value "${accountDateModifiedValue3}" should be different from the "${accountDateModifiedValue4}"

Scenario: Delete assigned customer contact role
	Customer contact roles assigned to contacts should not be able to be Deleted

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles
	| Default Account Customer Role |
	Then I should be able to view an error when I attempt to delete an assigned contact role on koroneiki with the name "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Default Account Customer Role"